tlock — provenance note
========================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling
`bls12_381`/`bbs`/`vdf`/`bulletproofs`/`bn254` modules — self-contained
crypto modules not folded into the root `NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

**Design reference (source read, not ported)**: this module's
ciphersuite (`src/ciphersuite.zig`) and `Ciphertext` wire format
(`src/tlock.zig`) are transcribed from drand's own production Go
source, fetched 2026-07-16:

- `github.com/drand/drand` (Apache-2.0), `crypto/schemes.go`,
  `NewPedersenBLSUnchainedG1` (the `SigsOnG1ID` /
  `"bls-unchained-g1-rfc9380"` scheme — quicknet's actual scheme,
  confirmed live against `https://api.drand.sh/v2/beacons/quicknet/info`).
  Supplies: `dst_g1`/`dst_g2` (RFC 9380 DSTs), `beaconId`'s
  `SHA-256(BigEndian(round))` digest construction.
- `github.com/drand/kyber` (Apache-2.0/MIT dual), `encrypt/ibe/ibe.go`.
  Supplies: the `H1`/`H2`/`H3`/`H4` constructions
  (`h2_tag`/`h3_tag`/`h4_tag` = `"IBE-H2"`/`"IBE-H3"`/`"IBE-H4"`
  verbatim), `EncryptCCAonG2`/`DecryptCCAonG2`'s exact 6-step
  encrypt / 4-step decrypt BF-IBE FullIdent construction (`tlock.zig`'s
  module doc comment transcribes this construction into the doc
  contracts the `encrypt`/`decrypt` Fable cores implement — no source
  code copied, the ALGORITHM SHAPE was read and re-expressed).
- `github.com/drand/tlock` (Apache-2.0/MIT dual), `tlock.go`.
  Supplies: the `Ciphertext.toBytes`/`fromBytes` wire format (`U (96B
  G2 compressed) || V (16B) || W (16B)`, `cipherVLen`/`cipherWLen =
  16` — this module's `ciphersuite.block_bytes`), and the
  `TimeLock`/`TimeUnlock` scheme-dispatch confirming quicknet routes
  through `EncryptCCAonG2`/`DecryptCCAonG2` despite the `SigsOnG1ID`
  scheme name (see `ciphersuite.zig`'s module doc comment, "Variant
  confirmation" section).
- `github.com/drand/kyber-bls12381` (Apache-2.0/MIT dual),
  `kyber_g1.go`/`kyber_g2.go`/`kyber_gt.go`/`kyber_scalar.go`. Read to
  confirm: point serialization is compressed (matches
  `bls12_381.g1`/`g2`'s own `toBytesCompressed` convention); the `Gt`
  (`Fp12`) serialization is `kilic/bls12-381`'s `GT.ToBytes`, itself
  confirmed (via `github.com/kilic/bls12-381` `fp12.go`) to use the
  SAME high-to-low `c1 || c0` (576-byte) tower convention
  `bls12_381.Fp12.toBytes` already documents (byte NESTING now fully
  vector-verified — see the interop-vector section below; kilic's
  pairing VALUE, however, is the canonical value's CUBE, see
  `SPEC.md`'s "Gt serialization" section); the scalar
  field modulus (`curveOrder` in `kyber_scalar.go`) is confirmed
  byte-identical to `bls12_381.scalar.r_bytes`.

No source code from any of the above was copied into this module —
every construction was independently re-expressed in Zig from reading
the reference Go source, per `CONVENTIONS.md`'s "design reference"
category (prime directive 1: "model after a proven implementation in
another language"). All four repositories are Apache-2.0 or dual
Apache-2.0/MIT licensed; no GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or
copied anywhere in this module.

**Academic reference**: Boneh, D. and Franklin, M., "Identity-Based
Encryption from the Weil Pairing", CRYPTO 2001 (the "FullIdent"
construction, §4.2) — a public academic paper, not a copyrightable
implementation (merger doctrine, `CONVENTIONS.md` §5).

